{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpnSu8Z19t8mc3KbXhJf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, that's expected if you're on Vitest 5. The v5.0.0 release notes list \"Don't lookup config file from ancestor directories\" (#10428) as a breaking change. Vitest now only looks for a config file in the directory you run it from. Earlier versions searched parent folders, which is why it used to find your root config.\n\nTo fix it, do one of these:\n- Run Vitest from the repo root.\n- Point at the config directly: `vitest --config ../../vitest.config.ts`\n- Add a `vitest.config.ts` in `packages/foo`. Combine it with the root config using `mergeConfig`, or use `test.projects` at the root.\n\nSource: [Vitest v5.0.0 release notes](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases/tag/v5.0.0)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":488,"cache_read_input_tokens":5396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":488},"output_tokens":264,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f71c7f6-d20c-4381-80b7-4b5d45c4e406","uuid":"f7219481-d58f-496e-8c1c-6c56a8228f1b","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:39:22.876Z","request_id":"req_011CfpnStrSBeVYVq9abZtj1"}
